// Per-player capsule: spawned by the server when a client joins, OWNED by that client. The owning
// client drives it with WASD/Space (key C toggles player control — the free-fly camera releases
// those keys; V toggles first/third person), simulating it LOCALLY for full responsiveness; the
// claim stream carries the resulting body state to the server, validated by the Network/Validation
// plausibility gate. Everyone else sees it as a normal replica.
// ONE entity: an invisible rotation-locked capsule body with the skinned character as its render
// mesh. PlayerBody.dsl animates + yaws it from the entity's actual movement (position-delta based,
// so replicas on other clients animate too); a locked body never writes rot back, so the script's
// facing survives. Render Scale 0.0125 = authored 0.005 / entity 0.4; Position 0 -2 0 puts the
// model's origin at the capsule bottom.
Prefab netPlayerCapsule
	Scale 0.4
	Component Render
		ObjectContainer character
		Node ROOT
		Type SkinnedMesh
			Rig Humanoid
		Position 0 -2 0
		Scale 0.0125
	Component Animator
		Animator CharacterAnimator
	Component Script
		Path Scripts/PlayerBody.dsl
		Enabled true
	Component Physics
		Body Dynamic
		Shape Capsule
		Radius 1
		HalfHeight 1
		Density 120
		Friction 0.3
		Restitution 0
		LockRotation true
		ContactEvents true
	Component Network
